# interplay_memlive_alias_ordered: Two tasks over the same two guest pages, their work ordered only by barriers across two FIFOs and rung at once: task 1 on the root FIFO fills its shared buffer A and its private buffer P (written back: invalidateGuest and synchronize, 6); task 2 on the worker (child 2), behind a barrier on that exec's stamp, copies its A2 and P2 (P2 with invalidateHost) out; task 1, behind task 2's stamp, fills again; task 2, behind that, copies again with flags 0. The shared buffers are the same RAM in every setup, so task 2 sees both of task 1's fills. Task 2's private buffer is paged at its first read: in-process it is then a host copy that flags 0 never pages again, so its second read misses task 1's second fill; in the service it is the guest pages, and sees it (docs/testing.md section 6.10: detach resources).
